\details{
The National Scale Volume and Biomass system derives diameter from the derivative of its
equation-6 Kozak cumulative-volume ratio. \code{dib()} follows \code{NVB_DibAtHT}, and
\code{height_at_dib()} follows \code{NVB_HT2TOPDib}. \code{stem_volume()} follows the Table S5 cumulative
inside-bark ratio used for national biomass equations component volumes.

The diameter path uses source Tables S3 and S4. Cumulative volume uses Tables S1 and S5.
Accordingly, \code{stem_volume()} does not numerically integrate the displayed inside-bark
diameter curve.

The default package mode returns the outside-bark diameter computed internally by the national
biomass equations. With \code{options(merchandiser.compat = 'nvel')}, \code{\link[=dob]{dob()}} reproduces
CALCDIA's unassigned zero output.
}
\section{Status and missing values}{

Unknown equations, missing required measurements, and unavailable bark calculations return
missing quantities. \code{\link[=status_codes]{status_codes()}} lists the diagnoses.

\code{not_unique} retains the highest detected diameter crossing. Review the profile when this
occurs.
}

